3^4\\) simplifies the terms:\n     \\[\n     2^{29} + 3^4 \\cdot 3^{29}\n     \\]\n   - Now. the largest prime divisor is:\n     \\[\n     3^4 - 2^{29}\n     \\]\n\nGiven the terms:\n   - 34, 81 *\n   +16 =>\n   *3=2*(3)/3\n\nHence, the final answer is:\n\\boxed{3}",
